<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Steps and Cost</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Step counting</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The number of steps a Worker actually uses can differ from its step budget. Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.1 Step counting ‣ Appendix C Steps and Cost ‣ Unsupervised Tool Evolution for Coding Agents in Data-Lake Analytics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> therefore plots the accuracy of <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TEAL</span> and the baseline against the steps they actually use under each step budget. The horizontal axis is the mean number of steps per episode over three test repeats, and the vertical axis is the accuracy, so a curve closer to the upper left offers a better trade-off between accuracy and steps. As expected, the evolved tools let the Worker reach higher accuracy with fewer steps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.27327v1/steps_accuracy.svg" id="A3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/290;" width="476" height="290"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Accuracy versus mean Worker steps per test episode.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Cost accounting</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A step budget is a practical way to bound the cost and latency of an agent in deployment. A budget stated directly in tokens or in dollars is less practical, since the agent would spend extra tokens tracking how many it has already used. However, a step budget does not reflect the actual cost of an episode. We therefore also plot accuracy against the estimated cost per test episode in Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.2 Cost accounting ‣ Appendix C Steps and Cost ‣ Unsupervised Tool Evolution for Coding Agents in Data-Lake Analytics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
